= Underfitting =

== Overview ==
'''Underfitting''' occurs when a learned model fails to capture relevant structure needed for good task performance.

An underfit system often performs poorly even on training data and also performs poorly on new data.

== Causes ==
Underfitting can result from:

* an inadequate hypothesis class;
* excessive regularization;
* insufficient optimization;
* poor features or representation;
* missing variables;
* too little training;
* an objective that does not match the task.

== Capacity ==
A model can underfit because it is too restricted, but:

<pre>
underfitting ≠ small model by definition
</pre>

A large model can underfit when optimization fails or the representation/objective prevents learning relevant structure.

== Bias ==
In classical bias–variance analysis, strong systematic approximation error is often associated with high bias.

That is a useful model-specific analysis, not the definition of all underfitting.

